From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:37:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] End when the terminal's input closes instead of panicking

Problem: when the terminal goes away while Helix runs (on AROS: the Limpet
window is closed), the input stream yields an UnexpectedEof error, and
handle_terminal_events unwraps it: the editor thread panics.
Change: an end of terminal input ends the event loop, as a hang-up does;
the terminal is restored if it can be, and Helix exits. Unsaved changes are
lost, as with SIGHUP on other systems.
Repository: helix-editor/helix
Base: a05c151bb6e8e9c65ec390b0ae2afe7a5efd619b (tag 25.07.1)
Author: tomaszstaniak
Date: 2026-10-19
Platform scope: all targets (crossterm reports the end of input this way on any).
Upstream status: candidate (not submitted).
Verification: on AROS One 1.3, closing the Limpet 0.6.1 window while hx runs
ends hx and the window closes; before, the window stayed on "Closing:
waiting for process".
---
 helix-term/src/application.rs | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/helix-term/src/application.rs b/helix-term/src/application.rs
index 40faf2fb61a8cb31cf0f15dabf4e10689016f9a2..b21657f3a3cac6bf3cd3a19d4095ef4380c68e40 100644
--- a/helix-term/src/application.rs
+++ b/helix-term/src/application.rs
@@ -315,6 +315,12 @@ pub async fn event_loop_until_idle<S>(&mut self, input_stream: &mut S) -> bool
                     };
                 }
                 Some(event) = input_stream.next() => {
+                    // The terminal went away (its window was closed): end as
+                    // after a hang-up instead of panicking on the error.
+                    if matches!(&event, Err(err) if err.kind() == std::io::ErrorKind::UnexpectedEof) {
+                        log::info!("terminal input closed, quitting");
+                        return false;
+                    }
                     self.handle_terminal_events(event).await;
                 }
                 Some(callback) = self.jobs.callbacks.recv() => {
